            "review_title": "Review at Hannah Pub - Restaurant",
            "review_text": "BryInThai\n1 contribution\n0\nrude staff, horrible food\nMar 2020\nI went here as well because of the claim of Mexican food. When I arrived there were maybe 3 other tables, one of which was being really loud. I purposely sat a ways away from this table and then proceeded to be approached by no staff for 10 minutes or so, I really wanted Mexican food so I stood up and someone finally gave me a menu, as it turns out the table that was being really loud was in fact the owner and her foreign husband. \n\nI ordered the enchiladas only to have the plate and the silverware container slammed on my table by the loud owner and this is where the real fun began. My enchilada was tortilla filled with a mess of vegetables and exactly zero mexican flavor. The enchilada sauce was ketchup and the cheese on top was mozzarella. It was also cold which is amazing since I think at that point i was the only person eating there. \n\n I don't expect anyone in Vietnam to be an expert on Mexican food but there is literally nothing right about this setup. \n\nI could have, and should have left without paying because no one came to check on me or even glance in my direction from that point forward. Even when I was standing next to her table with money in my hand the owner didn't even pause her super loud voice long enough to acknowledge that I was ready to pay. \n\nHer attitude is as terrible as the food and with any luck people will steer clear of this place. Sometimes cheap isn't good and Hannah definitely is not good\nRead more\nWritten March 12, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
